PURPOSE
H11 reached an observational identifiability wall.

A true reusable developmental direction and a globally shared measurement artifact can be made to have:
- the same source agreement;
- the same temporal persistence;
- the same apparent structural stability.

If those observational statistics are matched,
passive observation cannot determine which apparent dimension deserves permanent hereditary capacity.

H12 tests the next identifiability source:

FUNCTIONAL CAUSAL CONSEQUENCE.

QUESTION
Can a candidate slow structural direction be validated by whether temporarily expressing that direction causally improves local function?

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- prove real Yggdrasil has a target-free local functional consequence signal;
- freeze a microprobe schedule;
- freeze a structural cost;
- establish a production matched-control mechanism;
- authorize biological or wet-lab implementation;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

