PRIMARY CAUSAL-CONTROL RESULT
H12 inherits the S7-S9 rule.

A structural microprobe should not receive credit merely because:

FUNCTION IMPROVED AFTER THE PROBE.

It needs an estimate of:

WHAT WOULD HAVE HAPPENED WHILE I WAITED / OBSERVED ANYWAY?

This connects slow hereditary structural growth directly to the same causal-control machinery used for:
- action credit;
- resource credit.

