PRIMARY CONTROL-INTEGRITY LIMIT
In this geometry,
action contamination of the matched structural control mainly creates:

FALSE NEGATIVE STRUCTURAL CREDIT.

As contamination rises,
the control subtracts true U benefit.

At full contamination,
the organism refuses all structural growth.

This is preferable to confidently structuralizing the artifact,
but it sacrifices useful capacity.

Do not generalize this failure direction to arbitrary geometries.

The general rule remains:

BAD CONTROL
INVALIDATES CAUSAL STRUCTURAL CREDIT.

