META-PRINCIPLE
Yggdrasil now encounters the same causal requirement at three adaptive layers.

BEHAVIORAL CREDIT:
did my action help?

RESOURCE CREDIT:
did collecting more evidence help?

STRUCTURAL CREDIT:
did allocating permanent representational capacity help?

All three can be fooled by passive environmental change.

All three therefore need:
- action identity;
- disturbance control;
- control trust;
- repeated evidence.

IMPORTANT LIMITATION
The local consequence signal remains synthetic.

H12 does NOT demonstrate a real target-free Yggdrasil functional consequence signal.

Therefore:
H12 closes an architectural identifiability question,
not the real-signal bridge.

DECISION
AR-H12 is POSITIVE WITH A CONTROL-INTEGRITY LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- observationally indistinguishable persistent structure can be separated by functional consequence;
- a true developmental dimension can earn permanent capacity through repeated randomized expression;
- an equally persistent artifact can be rejected;
- persistence gating suppresses noisy one-shot false structural writes;
- passive environmental improvement can corrupt structural causal credit;
- action-decoupled matched controls repair that confounding in the tested benchmark;
- contaminated controls can suppress legitimate structural growth.

Not demonstrated:

- real target-free functional consequence;
- real structural-expression microprobes;
- optimal probe amplitude;
- optimal structural-cost accounting;
- nonlinear candidate directions;
- multi-direction synergy;
- safe candidate probing in mature high-value tissue;
- real control topology for structural credit.

NEXT CLEAN QUESTION
AR-H13 — NON-ADDITIVE / COOPERATIVE STRUCTURAL UTILITY

H12 tests candidate directions one at a time.

But some useful representational structures may be non-additive.

Question:

What if:

dimension A alone
does not improve function,

dimension B alone
does not improve function,

but

A + B together
create a useful developmental representation?

A purely individual causal-growth gate would reject both.

Test:

- individually neutral / costly candidate directions;
- jointly useful pair;
- sequential one-at-a-time structural growth;
- bounded pairwise cooperative microprobes;
- resource cost of searching combinations;
- false cooperative growth under noise.

Desired:

recover genuinely cooperative structure
without turning permanent-memory search into combinatorial explosion.

Do not execute STAB-18-R1 during this lane.

